      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-01-04_WidnesExaminer_art0042" n="art0042">
        <head>TESTIFY TO EFFICACY OF CUTICURA REMEDIES</head>
        <p>TESTIFY TO EFFICACY OF CUTICURA REMEDIES</p>
        <p>"I have great pleasure in giving particulars cf two complete cures de- rived from the use of the Cuticura Remedies.</p>
        <p>"In my own case, for more than six months I was suffering from disorder on my scalp and in consequence was fast losing my hair. I was advised to give Cuticura Soap and Cuticura Ointment a trial, which luckily did. I adopted the treatment irescribed and at the end of one month was completely cured. This was at the beginning of 1905. Since that time my head has been restored to its normal state, and no further outbreak has occurred, and whenever I ha've had the opportunity I always recommend the Cuticura Remedies.</p>
        <p>"A member of our family periodically _suffered for nearly ten years from dry eczema on the hands. The fingers and palms split and cracked everywhere at the slightest movement. At such periods they were most painful as well as quite useless, and gloves were always obliged to ,be worn. Every possible remedy was tried, besides medical advice, blood mixtures, ointments. soaps, etc.; some of which gave slight relief for a time, but never perma- nently. Finally, she was advised to try Cuticura Soap and Cuticum Oint- ment, which we are thankful to say effected a complete cure, as she has had no recurrence of the trouble for the last three years. We are most happy to testify to the efficacy of the Cuticum Remedies in similar cases. Edward Allen, 65, Denmark Road, South Nor- wood, S. E., March 20, 1906."</p>
      </div>
