        <p>On Sundqv last an omen meetin' of the four top classes of the Sunday school was held, presided over by Mrs. .Tarns nolds. There was a large congregation Present, ten, i frill:, to the ronnlaritv of these meetings held once every three months. In a few well-chosen words lfra. T)ndrls evlierted all nresent to love one another, even as Christ had loved las. The Rev. F. VaughFin addressed the meeting, basing his remarks upon " The v-ilderness and the solitary place shall be clad for them : and the desert shall reinice and blossom as the rose." To a very able manner Miss L. Fairhurst rendered " Into Thy. hands." end "He WAS despised." Miss F. Tin-n- Sanq " There narne a little child to earth. lon,. u'n" and 7.4;5s L. Kendrick gave a recitation entitled " q.anta (Thalia." The service from beginning to end 'ilia an ling,lalinerl fin"neSS,r.flectinc, great credit on all conewmed. A enllection, which realized a satis- factory nmonnt Cl 15q.) Tcrtc *made at the close of the service in "44 of the Ne,v Ffymn Rook Fund. Mr. P. Atkinson nm.iaaed ta or,nniat„ On New Yolr's evenlo2, a bachelor's tea wee held in connection with the yonn.7 men's class. On entering the ' tea room, ono was surprised to see such a grand spread prervved wholly by the young meui. who no doubt mnst have snent a great amount of time and enerZll making preparation for RI persons to sit down to a sub- stantial lctife end fork tel. After tea ft, short concert was held, oreided over hy %tr. R. K -Toney (teacher of the class), musical items heing rendered by Mrs. F. Gray. Minces A. Oal,lev and F. Fellows. Messrs. N. Moss and R. idol for-I. (Tames were indulged in and a very enjoyable evening was spent. •.ist</p>
