      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-01-04_WidnesExaminer_art0086" n="art0086">
        <head>Two Months for Breaking a_ Window.</head>
        <p>Two Months for Breaking a_ Window.</p>
        <p>At the Borough Court on Thursity,James Quigley, 13, Smith-street, was charged with breaking a plate- glass window in the vaults of the Lion Hotel, doing damage to the amount of £2 ss. on Wednesday night. —Mr. Stott, a barman at the vaults, said prisoner picked up two glasses and hurled them at the window, but the window did not break. While witness was getting over the counter the prisoner hurled a third glass, which broke the window. Prisoner was then arrested. —Prisoner, when asked if he had anything to say, replied "It's all right."—The Chief Constable said prisoner had eight previous convictions against him.—Quigley was sent to gaol for two months with hard labour.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-01-04_WidnesExaminer_art0087" n="art0087">
        <head>PAINFUL SHOPPING.</head>
        <p>A PAINFUL SHOPPING.</p>
        <p>Afflicted by Nervous Disorders and Rheumatism she lost all strength. How Dr. Williams' Pink Pills Cured Her.</p>
        <p>Mr. Ashton, of Preston, Lancashire, has a vivid recollection of a chill she caught some time ago, for her health broke down completely, so that even the effort required to go shopping was too much for her. The chill, as is frequently the case, found out the weak spot in her constitution, the result being that her nervous system collapsed and Rheumatism and Kidney Disorders developed. In this state she remained quite lin despair until, hearing of important cures by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People, ale tried. these pills and happily regained health. " Eighteen months ago, following a chill," she told a reporter, who called at her home, 6., Simpson-street, Preston, "I suffered from acute pains in the back and shoulders. Every time I moved my arms the pain seized me in the hack. My blood felt chilled and a languid exhausted feeling haunted me. Only slight pains at first attacked my limbs, but, after a time,they increased terribly, and it was only with the greatest difficulty I could stoop. At night 1 could not sleep or if I dozed off I started at every sound. "So gradually my nervous system entirely broke down. Like most women I take an interest in the latest fashions displayed in the shop windows, but they ceased to have any attraction for me, I was so dejected and low. When I was out of doors I had attacks of dizziness with a sinking feeling round the heart; often I had to return home hastily. Food became distasteful, for after the lightest meal sharp pains cat through my chest and back. My strength went altogether. I became so weak, tired, and languid</p>
        <p>-Out of doors .. attacks of dizziness." that I was quite unfit for any exertion. My breathing was difficult, and at all times I trembled violently.</p>
        <p>• LOSING Hon: ALTOGETUER. "Then I found that I was suffering from serious disorders of the kidneys ; and, though I took many medicines, my complaints became aggravated. My eyes were sunken and heavy, and surrounded by heavy dark rings. " Acute rheumatism next attacked me, 'and I felt pains like hot needles passing through my legs. I was altogether losing hope when I read of some of the wonderful cures effected by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills, for Pale People. So I began to take these pills, and before long experienced a little relief. I con- tinued, and a decided and wonderful change c2nie over me. My blood became warm, and I felt a glow of health in my cheeks. My appetite improved, and I enjoyed my meals. All bodily pains disappeared, my strength returned, and outdoor exercise became a pleasure.</p>
